WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.248 --> 00:00:01.260
(soft music)

00:00:01.260 --> 00:00:02.093
- [Narrator] When it comes

00:00:02.093 --> 00:00:04.090
to electric vehicle manufacturing,

00:00:04.090 --> 00:00:06.683
few resources are as vital as lithium.

00:00:07.980 --> 00:00:09.260
Over the past decade,

00:00:09.260 --> 00:00:12.440
prospectors unearthed troves
of the lithium chemicals

00:00:12.440 --> 00:00:13.950
that power batteries,

00:00:13.950 --> 00:00:16.970
but the shift toward a cleaner
economy is accelerating

00:00:16.970 --> 00:00:19.033
and batteries play a central role.

00:00:20.270 --> 00:00:22.400
As a result, demand for lithium

00:00:22.400 --> 00:00:26.073
is expected to exceed supply through 2025.

00:00:27.420 --> 00:00:30.760
Car makers and analysts say
that more lithium is needed

00:00:30.760 --> 00:00:33.960
to produce more batteries
at a faster pace.

00:00:33.960 --> 00:00:35.840
And as China takes a leading role

00:00:35.840 --> 00:00:37.570
in the battery supply chain,

00:00:37.570 --> 00:00:39.250
the US government is trying

00:00:39.250 --> 00:00:41.563
to boost domestic supply of the metal.

00:00:42.470 --> 00:00:45.183
Here's how Lithium became
such a hot commodity.

00:00:47.490 --> 00:00:50.130
Lithium is scattered
not only across the US

00:00:50.130 --> 00:00:51.823
but the entire world.

00:00:53.290 --> 00:00:56.070
In the top lithium producing
country, Australia,

00:00:56.070 --> 00:00:58.730
miners excavate a
mineral called spodumene,

00:00:58.730 --> 00:00:59.980
which contains the metal.

00:01:01.050 --> 00:01:03.130
And in Chile and Argentina,

00:01:03.130 --> 00:01:06.050
companies extract lithium
from massive salt lakes

00:01:06.050 --> 00:01:07.873
by pumping water into the ground.

00:01:09.500 --> 00:01:12.180
The extracted metals are
mixed with other elements

00:01:12.180 --> 00:01:15.360
to produce compounds,
like lithium hydroxide

00:01:15.360 --> 00:01:16.473
and lithium carbonate.

00:01:17.630 --> 00:01:20.423
These compounds are a key
part of many batteries.

00:01:21.560 --> 00:01:25.360
Car makers and battery
researchers, like Dr. Guihua Yu

00:01:25.360 --> 00:01:29.010
value Lithium because of its
unique chemical properties.

00:01:29.010 --> 00:01:31.130
- With lithium ions being so small,

00:01:31.130 --> 00:01:34.760
they can be very easily
recharged, as they diffuse quickly

00:01:34.760 --> 00:01:37.060
during battery charge and discharge.

00:01:37.060 --> 00:01:39.290
Lithium ions are also very light weight,

00:01:39.290 --> 00:01:42.850
so batteries based on Lithium
ions can offer high energy

00:01:42.850 --> 00:01:45.110
meaning that a lot of energy can be packed

00:01:45.110 --> 00:01:48.600
in a small amount or
small volume of materials.

00:01:48.600 --> 00:01:49.770
- [Narrator] These two properties,

00:01:49.770 --> 00:01:51.910
energy density and rechargeability

00:01:51.910 --> 00:01:55.480
are the reason why lithium is
found in so many batteries.

00:01:55.480 --> 00:01:57.810
Inside of all batteries
are two major components,

00:01:57.810 --> 00:01:59.850
the cathode and the anode,

00:01:59.850 --> 00:02:01.810
compounds that contain lithium ions

00:02:01.810 --> 00:02:05.260
transfer from one components
when power is drawn down

00:02:05.260 --> 00:02:08.330
and they return when the
battery is recharging

00:02:08.330 --> 00:02:09.270
- [Guihau Yu] And they can be charged

00:02:09.270 --> 00:02:11.760
like hundreds or thousands of times

00:02:11.760 --> 00:02:15.130
so they have different kind
of degradation mechanism.

00:02:15.130 --> 00:02:17.880
But lithium ions are so small,
so they are very stable.

00:02:17.880 --> 00:02:19.700
So that's the reason why the lithium ions

00:02:19.700 --> 00:02:22.429
can offer at least a few years of use.

00:02:22.429 --> 00:02:23.262
(upbeat music)

00:02:23.262 --> 00:02:24.980
- [Narrator] Scientists have spent decades

00:02:24.980 --> 00:02:27.440
perfecting lithium based batteries.

00:02:27.440 --> 00:02:30.100
Lithium was discovered in 1817,

00:02:30.100 --> 00:02:31.730
but more than a century passed

00:02:31.730 --> 00:02:33.710
before businesses used the chemical

00:02:33.710 --> 00:02:35.083
in mainstream batteries.

00:02:36.170 --> 00:02:38.340
In the 1990s, Sony took advantage

00:02:38.340 --> 00:02:40.630
of new, lightweight lithium ion batteries

00:02:40.630 --> 00:02:43.490
in a design for a hand-held video camera.

00:02:43.490 --> 00:02:45.150
The result was the Handycam.

00:02:45.150 --> 00:02:46.300
A smash commercial hit.

00:02:47.170 --> 00:02:49.530
Shortly afterward, rechargeable batteries

00:02:49.530 --> 00:02:52.343
began to appear in
laptops and smartphones.

00:02:53.290 --> 00:02:55.180
And batteries are increasingly used

00:02:55.180 --> 00:02:57.703
in conjunction with wind and solar power.

00:02:58.730 --> 00:03:00.780
Analysts like Simon Moores point out

00:03:00.780 --> 00:03:02.610
that demand for the chemical is growing

00:03:02.610 --> 00:03:05.495
as companies build bigger,
battery-powered machines.

00:03:05.495 --> 00:03:08.290
- People need more lithium today,

00:03:08.290 --> 00:03:09.780
and in the future than in the past,

00:03:09.780 --> 00:03:12.640
because you're going from
lithium ion batteries

00:03:12.640 --> 00:03:14.810
the size of your mobile phone

00:03:14.810 --> 00:03:17.160
to lithium ion batteries
the size of your car.

00:03:17.160 --> 00:03:19.770
The entire chasse of an electric vehicle

00:03:19.770 --> 00:03:21.163
is a lithium ion battery.

00:03:21.163 --> 00:03:23.220
So there's an order of magnitude bigger,

00:03:23.220 --> 00:03:24.053
and as a result

00:03:24.053 --> 00:03:26.633
you need an order of
magnitude more lithium supply.

00:03:27.690 --> 00:03:29.090
- [Narrator] Which means
that mining companies

00:03:29.090 --> 00:03:32.050
around the world are
searching for lithium.

00:03:32.050 --> 00:03:33.018
In the United States,

00:03:33.018 --> 00:03:36.510
companies like Lithium
Americas and Piedmont Lithium

00:03:36.510 --> 00:03:38.760
are looking for metal-bearing
spodumene minerals

00:03:38.760 --> 00:03:40.033
in familiar places.

00:03:40.990 --> 00:03:41.823
In the past,

00:03:41.823 --> 00:03:44.530
lithium from the tin-spodumene
belt of the Carolinas

00:03:44.530 --> 00:03:46.790
was used in the production
of both medication,

00:03:46.790 --> 00:03:48.720
and nuclear weapons.

00:03:48.720 --> 00:03:50.360
Today prospectors are fanning out

00:03:50.360 --> 00:03:52.090
in search of new deposits here,

00:03:52.090 --> 00:03:55.283
as well as in Arkansas,
Nevada, and California.

00:03:56.370 --> 00:03:59.130
The search is based on
expectations of consumer demand

00:03:59.130 --> 00:04:00.303
for electric vehicles.

00:04:01.400 --> 00:04:04.800
- It takes 4 to 7 years
to build a lithium mine,

00:04:04.800 --> 00:04:07.330
it takes 24 months to
build a battery plant.

00:04:07.330 --> 00:04:08.820
These two parts of the supply chain,

00:04:08.820 --> 00:04:10.810
they don't live in the same time zones.

00:04:10.810 --> 00:04:13.190
And that is the major challenge,

00:04:13.190 --> 00:04:16.170
is matching the supply
when the demand is needed,

00:04:16.170 --> 00:04:19.133
and at present, the industry
has really failed to date.

00:04:20.320 --> 00:04:21.610
- [Narrator] Even though E.V. sales

00:04:21.610 --> 00:04:24.960
currently make up about 2%
of the U.S. auto market,

00:04:24.960 --> 00:04:28.670
that share is expected
to grow to 10% by 2025,

00:04:28.670 --> 00:04:30.083
according to Morgan Stanley.

00:04:31.110 --> 00:04:32.800
And policies coming out of Washington

00:04:32.800 --> 00:04:35.300
could further boost demand
for battery components.

00:04:36.280 --> 00:04:38.330
President Biden ordered a review

00:04:38.330 --> 00:04:41.400
of domestic supply chains
for critical products.

00:04:41.400 --> 00:04:44.210
That includes
semiconductors, key minerals,

00:04:44.210 --> 00:04:45.980
pharmaceuticals, and,

00:04:45.980 --> 00:04:47.130
- Advanced batteries

00:04:47.130 --> 00:04:49.860
like the ones used in electric vehicles.

00:04:49.860 --> 00:04:52.167
There's strong bipartisan support

00:04:52.167 --> 00:04:54.450
for fast reviews of these four areas

00:04:54.450 --> 00:04:56.730
because they're essential to
protecting and strengthening

00:04:56.730 --> 00:04:58.450
American competitiveness.

00:04:58.450 --> 00:04:59.860
- [Narrator] President Biden's emphasis

00:04:59.860 --> 00:05:03.670
on supply chain is driven
in part by geopolitics.

00:05:03.670 --> 00:05:07.330
When it comes to lithium,
only about 1% of global output

00:05:07.330 --> 00:05:10.610
is both mined and processed in the U.S.

00:05:10.610 --> 00:05:13.430
China unearths about 10%.

00:05:13.430 --> 00:05:15.530
China also processes about two thirds

00:05:15.530 --> 00:05:17.040
of the worlds lithium supply,

00:05:17.040 --> 00:05:19.113
and dominates the global battery market.

00:05:20.000 --> 00:05:21.210
The U.S. government has said

00:05:21.210 --> 00:05:23.190
that relying on oversea sources

00:05:23.190 --> 00:05:26.838
for these materials creates
a strategic vulnerability,

00:05:26.838 --> 00:05:28.960
which means that a new hunt for lithium

00:05:28.960 --> 00:05:31.030
is only getting started.

00:05:31.030 --> 00:05:33.950
The race is on to see who
will supply the world,

00:05:33.950 --> 00:05:36.033
with this powerful metal.

00:05:36.033 --> 00:05:38.450
(soft music)

